 "discussion": {
  "office": "SLC",
  "issued": "2026-11-28T05:49:00+00:00",
  "key_messages": "- Strong downslope winds are expected Saturday morning into Saturday afternoon across the Castle Country region, particularly from around Emery southward through Fremont Junction. Wind gusts of up to 50 to 60 mph can be expected for this area. - A weak storm system will move across northern Utah and southwest Wyoming late tonight into Saturday, bringing generally light valley rain and mountain snow. - Dry conditions will return temporarily on Sunday before another weak system grazes northern Utah on Monday. A more potent system may impact primarily southern Utah for the latter half of the upcoming week.",
